\f1\b \cf4 \cb3 The middle arrow is the invention.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 That's where I'd spend the research effort.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf4 \cb3 Not on proving the seven-dimensional cross product exists.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf4 \cb3 Not on admiring its exceptional symmetries.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf4 \cb3 On deriving a four-dimensional effective physical structure from the specific timespace interpretation you've assigned to its basis.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf4 \cb3 And importantly, the middle arrow has to do more than reproduce familiar equations by definition.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf4 \cb3 It must explain why those equations arise from the proposed structure.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
